Feature: Variable capture from Given steps
  Image: alpine

  Scenario: Save plain output as variable
    Given I run "echo hello"
    And I save output as $GREETING
    When I run "sh -c 'echo $GREETING'"
    Then the output should contain "hello"

  Scenario: Save JSON path as variable
    Given I run "echo '{\"version\":\"1.2.3\"}'"
    And I save JSON path "$.version" as $VERSION
    When I run "sh -c 'echo $VERSION'"
    Then the output should contain "1.2.3"

  Scenario: Save pattern as variable
    Given I run "sh -c 'echo v1.2.3'"
    And I save pattern "v([0-9.]+)" as $VERSION
    When I run "sh -c 'echo $VERSION'"
    Then the output should contain "1.2.3"

  Scenario: Use captured variable in file content
    Given I run "echo myapp"
    And I save output as $APPNAME
    And a file "hello.sh" with content:
      #!/bin/sh
      echo "Hello from $APPNAME"
    When I run "sh hello.sh"
    Then the output should contain "Hello from myapp"
